  "name": "Dotted Metal Stab",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "An off-beat pocket riddim: a metallic FM-flavoured square that opens and falls on a dotted-eighth cadence, so across two bars it drifts against the kick and lands back on the downbeat. Mono below, a little wide above. Play: F1, G1 and A#1 stabs or held notes with the transport running at 140-150 BPM, and leave gaps so the dotted pulse speaks. Macros: Stab Depth deepens the sweep on every pulse, FM Mix thickens the metallic FM, Notch Sweep moves the hollow notch and Width opens the chorus above the low end.",
